# THE RING BY DAY (19_orbit, src/render/orbit/): a pass staged overhead at noon,
# looked straight up at. The unlit hull is the sky's own colour -- a ghost of a
# wheel, the way the moon is by day -- asked of the live frame (`ring_ghost`:
# the unlit hull within a few levels of the open sky beside it), and the pass
# moves across the sky while it is watched.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/orbit_sky.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=12 --orbit=zenith@12 --eye=1.7,-80,70 --face=146 --weather=clear:0
wait 2
await ring 5
await ring_ghost 5
shot 00-noon-ghost
wait 3
shot 01-noon-moving
wait 3
shot 02-noon-moving
